WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:30.110 --> 00:01:33.490
<b>Windmill Village,
East Blue</b>

3
00:01:33.810 --> 00:01:35.160
How is that possible?

4
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:37.270
They left Garp
on Pirate Island?

5
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:38.500
What happened to him?

6
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.080
The article says he went there
to rescue some guy named Koby.

7
00:01:42.160 --> 00:01:43.350
I guess he succeeded.

8
00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:44.940
Too bad it cost him his life.

9
00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:46.820
Where does it say he's dead?

10
00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:48.380
The man's a living legend.

11
00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:50.030
This isn't how he's gonna go.

12
00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.900
Wipe those looks
off your faces?

13
00:01:51.980 --> 00:01:52.730
You're right.

14
00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:53.810
I'm sure he's fine.

15
00:01:53.890 --> 00:01:55.630
Damn right he is.

16
00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.370
Who's laughing?

17
00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:01.110
You think this is funny?

18
00:02:03.290 --> 00:02:04.710
Oh, sweetheart.

19
00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:06.030
Don't worry.

20
00:02:06.110 --> 00:02:07.370
He didn't mean it.

21
00:02:07.450 --> 00:02:08.290
There, there.

22
00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.200
Oh, it was just the baby.

23
00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:11.380
I'm sorry, Makino.

24
00:02:11.940 --> 00:02:14.410
You're worried about
Garp too, aren't you?

25
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:16.540
Was that what you
were laughing at?

26
00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:18.200
"Straw Hats' Hostage Situation"

27
00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:18.810
You know Luffy's
face now, don't you?

28
00:02:18.890 --> 00:02:20.000
We love Luffy.

29
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:21.050
Yes, we do.

30
00:02:24.830 --> 00:02:27.180
What the hell are
those idiots thinking?

31
00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:36.220
<b>Hostage Situation</b>

32
00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.150
Oh, we got a big one!

33
00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:49.380
Help!

34
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.940
<b>East Blue</b>

35
00:02:51.650 --> 00:02:52.940
It's an earthquake!

36
00:03:00.330 --> 00:03:02.830
<b>South Blue</b>

37
00:03:05.750 --> 00:03:07.750
<b>West Blue</b>

38
00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:07.520
Follow me!

39
00:03:07.600 --> 00:03:08.500
We have to go!

40
00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:13.260
<b>North Blue</b>

41
00:03:13.460 --> 00:03:14.600
What's happening?

42
00:03:16.510 --> 00:03:25.600
<b>The earthquake on that day
was unprecedented in recorded history.


It left severe damage
in its wake across the world.</b>

43
00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:21.600
The earthquake on that day was
unlike any other in recorded history.

44
00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:25.660
It caused devastating
damage all around the world.

45
00:03:26.600 --> 00:03:28.560
<b>Grand Line</b>

46
00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:39.920
No, we're too late...

47
00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.140
The situation was
highly unusual.

48
00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:51.120
The earthquake's epicenter
could not be detected.

49
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:53.390
The truth was hidden
from the public.

50
00:03:53.470 --> 00:03:57.660
But it was no coincidence that the tragedy
occurred six days after the kingdom of

51
00:03:57.740 --> 00:04:00.560
Lulusia was wiped off the map
by the World Government.

52
00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.640
I'm at the remains of Lulusia!

53
00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.980
There is no trace
of the land anymore!

54
00:04:05.060 --> 00:04:07.730
Just a giant hole
swallowing up the sea!

55
00:04:08.180 --> 00:04:10.190
No further approach
is possible!

56
00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.700
The hole isn't filling!

57
00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:19.120
Across the entire world, sea levels Rose
by approximately one meter following the

58
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.720
havoc of the earthquake.

59
00:04:22.840 --> 00:04:25.080
The beach has never
flooded like this!

60
00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.480
At this rate, there won't be
any beach left here at all!

61
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:34.500
Why isn't the tide
pulling back?

62
00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:36.500
This is too cruel!

63
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.170
Running on the beach
is our favorite pastime!

64
00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:42.740
Give it back!

65
00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.930
This isn't glamorous at all!

66
00:04:45.010 --> 00:04:52.630
A number of beaches have disappeared
from the world, along with several islands.

67
00:04:54.700 --> 00:04:56.680
There's nothing
left for us here!

68
00:04:56.760 --> 00:04:57.690
We have to go!

69
00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.970
My sharks swim
right into my house!

70
00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:04.250
It's not supposed
to be high tide yet!

71
00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:06.170
Might make for a big
catch, though.

72
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.780
You really want to go
sailing in this mess?

73
00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.060
Sir, an update
on the flooding situation.

74
00:05:14.980 --> 00:05:17.610
Sea levels are rising
around the world.

75
00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:18.880
Yes, sir.

76
00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.460
But the cause is unclear.

77
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:26.930
Meanwhile, Egghead was surrounded by
a fleet of 100 Navy vessels of various

78
00:05:27.010 --> 00:05:30.130
sizes, including 20
massive battleships.

79
00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:34.640
This was a force that could level a nation,
with power far exceeding even

80
00:05:34.720 --> 00:05:35.820
that of a Buster Call.

81
00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:39.590
The total number
of marines was 30,000.

82
00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.030
And the leaders of
this unprecedented operation...

83
00:05:49.920 --> 00:05:53.260
...were nine Navy
HQ Vice-Admirals...

84
00:05:59.480 --> 00:06:01.460
...and Admiral Kizaru.

85
00:06:05.170 --> 00:06:06.630
We're under attack!

86
00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:43.870
Hey!

87
00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.490
I told you not to attack
the sea beast's weapons!

88
00:06:48.220 --> 00:06:49.070
I heard you.

89
00:06:49.150 --> 00:06:51.760
But I'm afraid it
attacked us first.

90
00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:55.010
Your meal is served, sir.

91
00:06:57.030 --> 00:06:58.680
Oh, my favorite.

92
00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:00.450
There you go!

93
00:07:00.530 --> 00:07:01.820
Eat it while it's hot!

94
00:07:09.490 --> 00:07:13.370
I gotta say, you're really putting
me on the spot here, Sentomaru.

95
00:07:14.930 --> 00:07:18.700
Why don't you just surrender and have
a nice bowl of ramen with me?

96
00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.810
Get serious!

97
00:07:19.890 --> 00:07:22.160
Attack again
and we'll open fire!

98
00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.300
Ooh, now you're scaring me.

99
00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.370
You know what you're
up against here!

100
00:07:26.450 --> 00:07:30.510
Punk developed the pacifista's
lasers by studying your power!

101
00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.390
Wow!

102
00:07:33.220 --> 00:07:34.020
So cool!

103
00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:36.110
Now you're here
to murder him.

104
00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:38.440
Never thought things
would turn out this way.

105
00:07:38.480 --> 00:07:41.220
He studied the Void
Century, Sentomaru.

106
00:07:41.300 --> 00:07:44.370
Old friend or not, I can't
defend a crime like that.

107
00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:48.290
In the end, I'm just
the Navy's puppet.

108
00:07:50.010 --> 00:07:53.750
That said, we don't want to have
this battle any more than you do.

109
00:07:53.830 --> 00:07:56.400
The more we destroy,
the more we lose.

110
00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.650
I was really hoping Lucci would clean
this up quickly without me.

111
00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.040
Stop trashing the place.

112
00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:04.590
You can thank the Straw
Hats for that one.

113
00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:08.260
<b>On a Battleship...</b>

114
00:08:09.710 --> 00:08:12.060
Don't let anyone
else know I'm here.

115
00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:12.950
Yes, sir.

116
00:08:13.640 --> 00:08:18.450
The Straw Hats took Vegapunk hostage
and barricaded themselves inside.

117
00:08:18.890 --> 00:08:20.340
I like this article.

118
00:08:21.100 --> 00:08:22.360
It's Morgan's work.

119
00:08:22.820 --> 00:08:24.430
And what is the truth?

120
00:08:24.510 --> 00:08:28.510
Sir, we haven't received word that
CP0 has completed their mission.

121
00:08:29.160 --> 00:08:32.690
Sentomaru is prepared
to defend the island outside.

122
00:08:32.770 --> 00:08:35.110
So we can guess who's
in the Labophase.

123
00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:39.300
First, we have Dr. Vegapunk
along with his six satellites.

124
00:08:40.090 --> 00:08:43.290
They should have the four
seraphim protecting them.

125
00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:48.250
Then there's Straw Hat Luffy and his crew,
who seem to have allied with the Doctor.

126
00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:55.480
Also, there's CP0's Rob Lucci,
along with the others in his leading unit,

127
00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.010
Kaku and Stussy.

128
00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:01.410
As for the other Cipher Pol agents,
they appear to have been captured by

129
00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.260
Sentomaru and
his pacifistas as well.

130
00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.620
They're probably
in the Fabriophase.

131
00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:07.320
One added note.

132
00:09:07.920 --> 00:09:13.050
The Frontier Dome's barrier status is
currently at 100%, meaning that no one

133
00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.780
can enter or leave
the Labophase.

134
00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:17.470
It's been like that
for an entire day.

135
00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:20.080
We still don't know
what's going on inside.

136
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:25.320
What happened to all the research staff
and technicians who were employed on

137
00:09:25.400 --> 00:09:26.100
Egghead?

138
00:09:26.890 --> 00:09:27.950
They're not present.

139
00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:30.150
They evacuated
the island yesterday.

140
00:09:30.230 --> 00:09:32.240
We've already
located their ships.

141
00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.440
And what if they
know too much?

142
00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:37.510
Sink them at once.

143
00:09:37.590 --> 00:09:38.390
Yes, sir.

144
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:40.710
Just one more thing first.

145
00:09:41.220 --> 00:09:42.970
We spotted Jewelry Bonney.

146
00:09:43.050 --> 00:09:45.470
She may be there
with the Straw Hats.

147
00:09:45.550 --> 00:09:47.460
Kuma's daughter, you say?

148
00:09:47.540 --> 00:09:49.960
We have no more use for her.

149
00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:51.510
Forget about her.

150
00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.180
She's just a girl.

151
00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:54.100
Yes, sir.

152
00:09:57.450 --> 00:09:58.310
Admiral, sir!

153
00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:01.280
What?

154
00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.540
I'm trying to enjoy
a meal here.

155
00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:06.910
We're picking up a signal
coming from Egghead.

156
00:10:06.910 --> 00:10:07.710
A signal?

157
00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:10.530
They seem to be making
a call somewhere.

158
00:10:10.610 --> 00:10:13.020
We'll find out who
they're calling, then.

159
00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:18.800
It's Mary Geoise!

160
00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:20.600
<b>Mary Geoise
The Holy Land</b>

161
00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:25.150
Who is this?

162
00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:29.890
Admiral, you should have a black
transponder snail on your wrist.

163
00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:30.950
Oh.

164
00:10:31.030 --> 00:10:32.390
You can tap the call.

165
00:10:32.470 --> 00:10:33.300
Whoa.

166
00:10:42.710 --> 00:10:43.560
Yeah, hello?

167
00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:44.270
It's me.

168
00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:45.290
York!

169
00:10:45.370 --> 00:10:46.750
You're still alive.

170
00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.490
That's all you have to say?

171
00:10:48.570 --> 00:10:49.850
Are you kidding me?

172
00:10:49.930 --> 00:10:52.090
Why the hell are you
trying to kill me, too?

173
00:10:50.750 --> 00:10:55.890
<b>Room of Authority</b>

174
00:10:52.090 --> 00:10:54.390
I'm the one who told
you what Stella did.

175
00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:55.870
Remember that, Peapaws?

176
00:10:56.280 --> 00:11:00.990
Be that as it may, you're still
a Vegapunk, just like the others.

177
00:11:01.070 --> 00:11:03.880
I don't give a shit about
the Void Century!

178
00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:06.060
And even if I did, you think
I would have taken it?

179
00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:07.850
Tipped you off about it?

180
00:11:07.930 --> 00:11:08.730
Use your brains!

181
00:11:10.530 --> 00:11:11.710
Fair enough.

182
00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:13.640
But how did you survive?

183
00:11:13.720 --> 00:11:16.090
Did CP0 fail at their mission?

184
00:11:16.430 --> 00:11:18.980
And what is the status
of the Straw Hats?

185
00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:23.070
Well, I'm still here.

186
00:11:23.150 --> 00:11:25.810
That alone should tell
you how the others are?

187
00:11:25.890 --> 00:11:28.190
I'm the one calling
the shots now!

188
00:11:29.220 --> 00:11:31.180
And Egghead is mine.

189
00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.450
All mine!

190
00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:39.910
About your little fleet
surrounding the island...

191
00:11:42.030 --> 00:11:44.800
You trying to start a war
with me or something?

192
00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.440
We could be convinced
to alter our plans, York.

193
00:11:49.940 --> 00:11:51.970
But let me confirm
one thing first.

194
00:11:52.050 --> 00:11:54.300
Can you create the Mother
Flame yourself?

195
00:11:59.960 --> 00:12:02.340
Oh, now they
want to negotiate.

196
00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.410
I'm glad I sent
you that sample.

197
00:12:04.490 --> 00:12:07.140
I knew you'd get hooked
once you had a piece.

198
00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.700
It is of the highest priority.

199
00:12:10.040 --> 00:12:12.320
Whose priority, I wonder?

200
00:12:12.400 --> 00:12:15.750
Too bad this island's the only
power plant that makes it.

201
00:12:25.710 --> 00:12:27.030
Here's the sitch.

202
00:12:27.520 --> 00:12:32.010
Promise that me and the lab will make
it out of this thing unscathed.

203
00:12:32.480 --> 00:12:33.460
Agreed.

204
00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.340
And make me a Celestial Dragon
while you're at it.

205
00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:37.450
It shall be done.

206
00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:40.770
Then we've got
ourselves a deal.

207
00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.700
One more thing.

208
00:12:43.940 --> 00:12:46.500
I need you to come
and save me!

209
00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:49.300
Straw Hat Luffy is here!

210
00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:53.730
What?

211
00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:54.540
What's this?

212
00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.010
What's going on in there?

213
00:12:59.420 --> 00:13:00.460
Hey, Luffy.

214
00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.470
What should we
do with this one?

215
00:13:03.550 --> 00:13:05.480
No more use
for her now, right?

216
00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:08.890
Blast them all dead!

217
00:13:08.970 --> 00:13:10.400
No!

218
00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:11.480
Do it now, please!

219
00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:14.970
What a disaster this has been!

220
00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:17.010
I've caused you
all such trouble.

221
00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:17.920
Sorry.

222
00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.270
We forgive you,
but she is a different story.

223
00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:23.930
So, Luffy, what's
the plan for her?

224
00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:27.790
They want to keep
her alive, right?

225
00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.710
Let's use her as a shield
when we run away.

226
00:13:30.800 --> 00:13:33.170
So it's like a hostage
situation, huh?

227
00:13:33.870 --> 00:13:34.860
Talk to me, Doc.

228
00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:35.980
Is she gonna be okay?

229
00:13:35.980 --> 00:13:40.680
It'll take time for her wounds to heal,
but with plenty of rest, she'll be fine.

230
00:13:43.000 --> 00:13:43.800
Hello!

231
00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:46.390
Hello!

232
00:13:46.760 --> 00:13:49.730
My name is... Monkey D.

233
00:13:49.820 --> 00:13:50.530
Luffy!

234
00:13:50.620 --> 00:13:52.740
And I'm gonna be
King of the Pirates!

235
00:13:52.820 --> 00:13:54.150
That's what you
choose to open with?

236
00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:55.480
What is wrong with you?

237
00:13:55.570 --> 00:13:57.440
We have Dr. Vegapunk.

238
00:13:57.530 --> 00:13:59.450
All the Vegapunks, even!

239
00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:04.000
If you want to save York's life,
clear your ships from the shore!

240
00:14:04.470 --> 00:14:06.230
Every last one!

241
00:14:06.310 --> 00:14:07.990
You don't understand!

242
00:14:07.990 --> 00:14:09.340
Straw Hat is a monster!

243
00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:10.250
Straw Hat!

244
00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:13.020
He's torturing her!

245
00:14:13.020 --> 00:14:14.770
The rumors are true!

246
00:14:14.850 --> 00:14:15.900
He's a menace!

247
00:14:15.920 --> 00:14:18.460
<b>World Economic News</b>

248
00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.850
What is he doing?

249
00:14:18.940 --> 00:14:19.640
No!

250
00:14:19.730 --> 00:14:21.050
Luffy, why?

251
00:14:21.140 --> 00:14:22.600
That story was fake!

252
00:14:22.990 --> 00:14:25.140
So you're Straw
Hat Luffy, are you?

253
00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:27.880
Have you suffered any
casualties in the lab?

254
00:14:27.970 --> 00:14:29.780
Who is still there with you?

255
00:14:31.250 --> 00:14:33.200
Well, uh, let me see.

256
00:14:33.280 --> 00:14:34.720
A couple of people are hurt...

257
00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:35.730
Luffy, come on!

258
00:14:37.990 --> 00:14:38.580
Galick.

259
00:14:38.580 --> 00:14:39.550
Hmm?

260
00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:41.050
A woman's voice.

261
00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.200
Must be Nico Robin.

262
00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:45.380
Why'd you make me hang up?

263
00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:46.850
Intel is a weapon.

264
00:14:47.390 --> 00:14:49.880
You must never give
it to your enemies.

265
00:14:49.960 --> 00:14:50.660
Oh, right.

266
00:14:50.730 --> 00:14:51.440
Sorry.

267
00:14:51.520 --> 00:14:54.160
But hey, the ships
will be gone now, huh?

268
00:14:54.240 --> 00:14:55.240
Like hell they will!

269
00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.450
You think the Navy's
that dumb?

270
00:14:59.720 --> 00:15:01.060
What's our next move?

271
00:15:01.140 --> 00:15:03.550
There are three things
we must protect.

272
00:15:03.630 --> 00:15:04.930
York's safety.

273
00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:08.190
The data stored
inside Punk Records.

274
00:15:08.860 --> 00:15:11.800
And the power plant that
creates the Mother Flame.

275
00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:14.480
Everything else is expendable.

276
00:15:15.800 --> 00:15:20.290
But sir, Rob Lucci and the other Cipher
Pol agents are still trapped inside there.

277
00:15:20.370 --> 00:15:22.650
We might face
a worst-case scenario.

278
00:15:23.090 --> 00:15:25.580
We must prioritize
accordingly.

279
00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:30.150
Regard humans as
you regard insects.

280
00:15:30.230 --> 00:15:33.850
Even if you exterminate some,
they'll multiply again.

281
00:15:33.930 --> 00:15:34.730
Hmm...

282
00:15:35.770 --> 00:15:36.600
Hmm...

283
00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:39.880
Yes, sir.

284
00:15:41.110 --> 00:15:43.490
You listen to me,
you tiny terrorists!

285
00:15:43.570 --> 00:15:46.420
I made a pact with the Five
Elders, you get it?

286
00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:48.050
Hurt me and you die!

287
00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:51.900
What they do to this island
will make Ohara look like fireworks!

288
00:15:58.510 --> 00:15:59.340
That hurt!

289
00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:04.810
You're gonna pay!

290
00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:07.510
I'll sic the Elders on you first!

291
00:16:07.590 --> 00:16:08.080
Yeah?

292
00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:09.030
Go right ahead.

293
00:16:09.860 --> 00:16:11.490
You're lucky that's all you got!

294
00:16:11.570 --> 00:16:13.670
How dare you say
that in front of Robin!

295
00:16:13.750 --> 00:16:15.680
Keep your filthy mouth shut!

296
00:16:16.460 --> 00:16:17.880
She can't hurt us.

297
00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:18.930
Just ignore her.

298
00:16:19.790 --> 00:16:22.140
Robin, are you feeling okay?

299
00:16:22.640 --> 00:16:23.460
Of course.

300
00:16:23.540 --> 00:16:24.990
Have you met my doctor?

301
00:16:25.070 --> 00:16:25.820
He's brilliant.

302
00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:28.630
That doesn't make me
happy at all, you jerk!

303
00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:30.950
Hmph.

304
00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:32.360
Pretty pathetic display.

305
00:16:33.620 --> 00:16:36.860
Though to be fair, I was
fighting two seraphim at once.

306
00:16:39.320 --> 00:16:40.680
You need to rest.

307
00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:43.620
Shaka!

308
00:16:45.360 --> 00:16:46.190
Pythagoras!

309
00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:47.800
Edison!

310
00:16:48.450 --> 00:16:49.980
Actually, I'm still alive.

311
00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:55.950
Could you quiet
down for a sec?

312
00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:56.480
What?

313
00:16:56.480 --> 00:16:59.710
I'm trying to get in contact
with the basement right now.

314
00:17:01.740 --> 00:17:03.070
Hey, can you guys hear me?

315
00:17:03.150 --> 00:17:04.500
Everyone's still alive?

316
00:17:05.160 --> 00:17:06.650
Thank you, Straw Hats!

317
00:17:06.730 --> 00:17:07.530
Heh heh heh.

318
00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:13.600
<b>Basement, Labophase</b>

319
00:17:08.020 --> 00:17:10.680
We can finally eat again!

320
00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:11.920
You saved us!

321
00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.430
We were losing hope!

322
00:17:13.850 --> 00:17:15.140
So good!

323
00:17:15.220 --> 00:17:16.340
I'm alive!

324
00:17:16.420 --> 00:17:21.240
Man, do I love
the Straw Hat crew!

325
00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.160
Hey, don't laugh, buddy.

326
00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:24.550
We're still enemies.

327
00:17:24.630 --> 00:17:27.320
Now, is there any chance you
could let us out of this room?

328
00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:31.200
I'm glad everyone's okay, but we
really can't do that right now, sorry.

329
00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.990
Fair enough,
but could you relocate us?

330
00:17:34.070 --> 00:17:36.090
It's kinda
nerve-wracking in here.

331
00:17:36.170 --> 00:17:37.380
With them around.

332
00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:38.170
What's wrong?

333
00:17:38.250 --> 00:17:40.600
Are you guys afraid
of the seraphim?

334
00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:43.360
They're supposed to be on the same
side as you guys, aren't they?

335
00:17:43.360 --> 00:17:44.230
And now?

336
00:17:44.310 --> 00:17:46.710
What if they go berserk?

337
00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:49.100
Hey, there's nothing
to worry about, is there?

338
00:17:49.180 --> 00:17:50.680
No, they're safe.

339
00:17:50.760 --> 00:17:55.330
Those bubble balls are made of the same
material as the pacifista Mark III's

340
00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:56.610
bubble shields.

341
00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.820
They're resilient enough
to deflect Cannon blasts.

342
00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:05.650
They're also created with sea energy,
making them the perfect prison to contain

343
00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.700
those with devil fruit powers.

344
00:18:07.780 --> 00:18:10.800
Oh, I thought they were
just regular bubbles.

345
00:18:11.520 --> 00:18:13.980
How dare you trap
me in this damn thing!

346
00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.380
It is foolish to be afraid of us.

347
00:18:17.470 --> 00:18:21.670
We do our job, and none of the seraphim
were ordered to kill you.

348
00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:23.510
You're of no interest to us!

349
00:18:24.150 --> 00:18:27.310
Well then, now I just feel silly.

350
00:18:27.980 --> 00:18:29.860
Don't mind the suits,
eh, Snake?

351
00:18:29.940 --> 00:18:30.940
They're just chompy.

352
00:18:30.990 --> 00:18:34.080
You're super cool in our book
after what you did before.

353
00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:37.020
Thanks for turning us back
from stone, little snake.

354
00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:38.580
She really did that?

355
00:18:39.110 --> 00:18:39.910
How peculiar.

356
00:18:40.360 --> 00:18:44.530
Unless I made an error, that behavior
should not be in the programming.

357
00:18:46.460 --> 00:18:47.090
Come on!

358
00:18:47.090 --> 00:18:48.320
Please, Hancock!

359
00:18:48.410 --> 00:18:49.570
They're my friends!

360
00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.920
You gotta undo
this stone thing now!

361
00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.360
You're the only person
who can save them!

362
00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:55.140
So please!

363
00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.170
Alright, fine!

364
00:18:59.950 --> 00:19:00.950
I will do it!

365
00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:03.760
Just please stop
staring at me like that!

366
00:19:04.740 --> 00:19:06.610
Oh, I see how it is.

367
00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:11.420
She's just as unmanageable as the original
Hancock, with the same soft spot for

368
00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.140
Luffy!

369
00:19:12.140 --> 00:19:13.460
This is too funny!

370
00:19:15.060 --> 00:19:17.710
I didn't know seraphim
worked that way!

371
00:19:17.790 --> 00:19:19.090
Oh, hi, Hancock!

372
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.070
How's it going?

373
00:19:21.150 --> 00:19:25.100
It seems the information transmitted
through bloodline elements is broader than

374
00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:25.830
I thought.

375
00:19:25.910 --> 00:19:26.840
Fascinating.

376
00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:29.170
You were super
awesome back there!

377
00:19:29.250 --> 00:19:31.550
I owe you!

378
00:19:34.010 --> 00:19:34.810
What?

379
00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:36.950
Did you just say I love you?

380
00:19:44.230 --> 00:19:46.050
Hey, Stella, we've got trouble.

381
00:19:46.520 --> 00:19:50.540
The communication system's been fully
restored, but the Frontier Dome still

382
00:19:50.620 --> 00:19:52.050
won't open for some reason.

383
00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:54.860
Don't even bother.

384
00:19:55.960 --> 00:19:58.040
I protected the Dome
with a passcode,

385
00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.920
but my brain's not synced
with all of you anymore.

386
00:20:01.010 --> 00:20:02.620
And I'm not telling!

387
00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:03.450
Oh, yeah?

388
00:20:05.370 --> 00:20:06.880
Alright, beat it!

389
00:20:06.880 --> 00:20:07.710
Lilith, no!

390
00:20:10.860 --> 00:20:13.830
While all of you lose your minds,
I'm gonna rest easy.

391
00:20:13.910 --> 00:20:16.160
Now, go fetch me a snack.

392
00:20:17.510 --> 00:20:18.900
Snack on my fist, you pig!

393
00:20:18.980 --> 00:20:21.830
If we can't deactivate the barrier,
then we can't escape.

394
00:20:21.860 --> 00:20:25.550
After all my smooth talking,
I thought we were free.

395
00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:27.390
Yeah, you're a real diplomat.

396
00:20:35.040 --> 00:20:36.670
Four seriously injured.

397
00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:39.250
Two of Vegapunk's
satellites dead.

398
00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:41.320
As for the straw hats...

399
00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:43.160
You're mumbling.

400
00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.150
What's wrong?

401
00:20:45.570 --> 00:20:47.130
Just talking to myself.

402
00:20:50.300 --> 00:20:54.300
I checked outside and we're
completely surrounded in all directions.

403
00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:55.770
Hello, Stussy!

404
00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.160
It looks like 100 ships.

405
00:20:58.240 --> 00:21:00.870
I'd assume there are
around 30,000 marines.

406
00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:03.350
My, this is quite ze event.

407
00:21:03.430 --> 00:21:05.190
Welcome back, my darling!

408
00:21:05.980 --> 00:21:07.800
Care for a cup of coffee?

409
00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:09.200
Why, thank you.

410
00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.460
Stop glaring at me.

411
00:21:12.820 --> 00:21:14.410
You're Nami, correct?

412
00:21:14.490 --> 00:21:15.800
The cruise navigator?

413
00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:16.550
Uh-huh.

414
00:21:16.550 --> 00:21:17.560
That's me.

415
00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.160
How does our route look?

416
00:21:19.240 --> 00:21:24.200
Uh, the Log Pose hasn't recorded a signal,
but we still have one steady needle from

417
00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:25.000
Wano.

418
00:21:25.080 --> 00:21:27.260
Seems we'll be
going northeast.

419
00:21:27.340 --> 00:21:28.880
Ah, that would be Elbaph.

420
00:21:28.960 --> 00:21:29.660
Elbaph?

421
00:21:29.710 --> 00:21:30.510
Really?

422
00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:32.290
We're going?

423
00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:33.200
Finally?

424
00:21:33.830 --> 00:21:35.240
Guess so, yeah.

425
00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.580
And what's there?

426
00:21:38.630 --> 00:21:39.750
The Giants!

427
00:21:41.010 --> 00:21:42.110
♪ The Giants! ♪

428
00:21:42.670 --> 00:21:43.910
♪ The Giants! ♪

429
00:21:44.430 --> 00:21:46.870
Why are they so
excited about this?

430
00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:52.640
We do have one advantage.

431
00:21:52.720 --> 00:21:56.050
Your ship is up here in the Labophase,
within our grasp.

432
00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.840
The Navy ships are
offshore in all directions.

433
00:21:59.170 --> 00:22:02.150
It would be impossible
to sail out of the port.

434
00:22:02.230 --> 00:22:04.880
You said that we'll be heading
toward the northeast.

435
00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:07.510
That's the back
side of the island.

436
00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:11.340
Luckily, your ship is waiting right
next to the Vegaforce-01.

437
00:22:11.420 --> 00:22:15.350
With a little rocket propulsion,
it should be able to carry us clean

438
00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:16.650
over the Navy blockade.

439
00:22:16.190 --> 00:22:24.160
<b>Flight-Capable Airspace</b>

440
00:22:16.730 --> 00:22:21.190
On the downside, Vegaforce-01 can only
fly within the airspace over Egghead.

441
00:22:21.270 --> 00:22:24.540
So let's hope we get enough
distance before we take a nosedive.

442
00:22:24.620 --> 00:22:26.480
There's no way
that'll be far enough!

443
00:22:26.560 --> 00:22:27.740
I got you, Doc!

444
00:22:27.820 --> 00:22:31.330
You just do the best you can, then
the Sunny's coup de burst will carry us

445
00:22:31.330 --> 00:22:32.340
the rest of the way!

446
00:22:32.420 --> 00:22:34.230
We'll fly a whole kilometer!

447
00:22:34.310 --> 00:22:36.500
No way they'll
catch us after that!

448
00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:37.580
My goodness!

449
00:22:37.660 --> 00:22:40.100
How in the world
can your ship fly so far?

450
00:22:40.180 --> 00:22:42.370
Cola power, Vegabro!

451
00:22:42.450 --> 00:22:43.760
Cola power?

452
00:22:52.800 --> 00:22:53.570
I love it!

453
00:22:53.650 --> 00:22:54.990
That sounds like a plan!

454
00:22:55.070 --> 00:22:55.900
Ah, yeah!

455
00:22:57.180 --> 00:22:57.630
Lilith?

456
00:22:57.630 --> 00:22:59.840
Can you head to Vegaforce-01
now?

457
00:22:59.920 --> 00:23:01.320
I know what you're thinking.

458
00:23:01.340 --> 00:23:05.000
You want me to move the Straw Hat's
ship to the back side of the island, right?

459
00:23:05.000 --> 00:23:06.190
I'll help, you.

460
00:23:06.270 --> 00:23:08.210
But we still can't go
anywhere till we do that.

461
00:23:08.210 --> 00:23:10.030
We have to deactivate
the darn Frontier Dome!

462
00:23:10.030 --> 00:23:12.430
And I'm never gonna
hand over the code!

463
00:23:20.220 --> 00:23:21.190
We'll crack it!

464
00:23:21.270 --> 00:23:22.870
We'll crack the punk out of it!

465
00:23:25.190 --> 00:23:27.580
Seems like our plan is
coming together nicely.

466
00:23:27.660 --> 00:23:31.620
I bet there's absolutely zero chance
we pull this off without a hitch.

467
00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:35.700
That's all we got, and we
don't know till we try.

468
00:23:35.780 --> 00:23:37.680
Yeah, that's true enough.

469
00:23:38.100 --> 00:23:39.890
If you're going to the Sunny,
take me with.

470
00:23:39.890 --> 00:23:41.730
That is my baby, after all.

471
00:23:41.810 --> 00:23:42.810
Take me, too!

472
00:23:42.890 --> 00:23:44.790
I can't wait to see elbow!

473
00:23:44.870 --> 00:23:45.770
Hey!

474
00:23:45.850 --> 00:23:46.790
Let me help out!

475
00:23:48.050 --> 00:23:48.870
Oh, thank you.

476
00:23:51.090 --> 00:23:51.920
Ready?

477
00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.540
It's time to go!

478
00:24:09.960 --> 00:24:12.070
Let's get your ship
to the back side, quick!

479
00:24:12.070 --> 00:24:14.600
Knowing them, they'll have
that Frontier Dome down soon.

480
00:24:14.600 --> 00:24:15.550
That might be good.

481
00:24:15.620 --> 00:24:17.720
Or it might just cause
even more problems.

482
00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:18.450
I don't get it.

483
00:24:18.450 --> 00:24:19.970
Why wouldn't you
want it down?

484
00:24:20.050 --> 00:24:21.250
Cause there's the catch.

485
00:24:21.260 --> 00:24:23.560
If we can get out,
the Feds can get in.

486
00:24:23.640 --> 00:24:26.600
If we're not ready to rock
when it opens, we're in trouble.

487
00:24:26.680 --> 00:24:28.520
Oh, I see now.

488
00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:29.600
This is so much fun!

489
00:24:29.630 --> 00:24:31.440
I've never left Egghead!

490
00:24:31.520 --> 00:24:32.800
World, here I come!

491
00:24:32.880 --> 00:24:33.570
Come on, Doc!

492
00:24:33.570 --> 00:24:34.830
This ain't a road trip!

493
00:24:34.910 --> 00:24:37.490
I just thought of something.

494
00:24:38.950 --> 00:24:41.070
We're gonna need
so much more food!

495
00:24:41.150 --> 00:24:42.250
Oh yeah, you're right!

496
00:24:42.330 --> 00:24:43.940
We'll eat all of this in one day!

497
00:24:43.940 --> 00:24:45.190
Do we even have pizzas?

498
00:24:45.270 --> 00:24:45.760
Crap!

499
00:24:45.760 --> 00:24:46.600
That's super important!

500
00:24:46.600 --> 00:24:48.440
We have to get
a ton of cheese!

501
00:24:48.520 --> 00:24:51.450
I think we have everything else
Sanji needs to make them for us.

502
00:24:51.450 --> 00:24:52.250
Really?

503
00:24:52.850 --> 00:24:54.330
That guy's pretty cool, huh?

504
00:24:54.410 --> 00:24:56.410
He's a good cook
and a good fighter.

505
00:24:56.490 --> 00:24:57.430
Huh.

506
00:24:57.510 --> 00:24:58.640
This is weird.

507
00:24:58.720 --> 00:25:01.790
What's got you in such
a happy mood all of a sudden?

508
00:25:01.870 --> 00:25:04.280
Earlier you wanted
to kill Old Man Apple.

509
00:25:09.710 --> 00:25:10.450
You're right.

510
00:25:10.530 --> 00:25:11.270
I did.

511
00:25:11.350 --> 00:25:12.680
But I'm over that now.

512
00:25:14.520 --> 00:25:15.320
That's good.

513
00:25:16.120 --> 00:25:17.740
So why were you
crying all night?

514
00:25:17.740 --> 00:25:18.430
Hey, shut up!

515
00:25:18.430 --> 00:25:19.260
I was not!

516
00:25:21.150 --> 00:25:23.490
We received
a transmission from Lucci!

517
00:25:23.570 --> 00:25:26.040
We know the situation
inside the dome now.

518
00:25:29.460 --> 00:25:31.220
Share it with the other ships.

519
00:25:31.300 --> 00:25:32.100
Yes, sir!

520
00:25:38.860 --> 00:25:41.150
Did you hear that, Borsalino?

521
00:25:42.360 --> 00:25:43.270
Uh-huh.

522
00:25:43.910 --> 00:25:48.360
He talked a big game, but it seems he doesn't
have quite as much leverage as he implied.

523
00:25:49.000 --> 00:25:50.010
In fact...

524
00:25:50.090 --> 00:25:52.640
All of them are trapped
in that dome like rats.

525
00:25:52.720 --> 00:25:57.180
If it uses a laser defense system,
can't you simply pass through it?

526
00:25:57.260 --> 00:26:00.350
You are light itself,
are you not?

527
00:26:00.430 --> 00:26:02.740
Well, the barrier isn't
what's stopping me.

528
00:26:02.820 --> 00:26:06.420
There's a friend of mine waiting on the shore,
and he's determined to protect

529
00:26:06.420 --> 00:26:07.120
Vegapunk.

530
00:26:07.160 --> 00:26:09.260
Why not fly over him?

531
00:26:09.340 --> 00:26:12.730
I can't disrespect a man who's
putting everything on the line.

532
00:26:12.810 --> 00:26:14.990
I like to think I'm
cooler than that.

533
00:26:15.380 --> 00:26:18.260
At the very least, let me
stick to my principles.

534
00:26:19.080 --> 00:26:19.950
And remember...

535
00:26:20.030 --> 00:26:21.990
Sentomaru is
poised to attack.

536
00:26:22.070 --> 00:26:26.260
The second we make a move, he'll order
every resource at his command into action.

537
00:26:26.340 --> 00:26:30.150
That means a swarm of sea beast
weapons and fifty pacifistas.

538
00:26:30.230 --> 00:26:32.500
Bad news for all
the ships we brought.

539
00:26:33.190 --> 00:26:35.720
We'll be committing
to a massive bloodbath.

540
00:26:37.920 --> 00:26:39.810
We better settle this quickly.

541
00:26:40.780 --> 00:26:43.170
Do we know where
the power plant is?

542
00:26:47.450 --> 00:26:50.330
Our friend Lucci hasn't
been sleeping on the job.

543
00:26:51.270 --> 00:26:55.860
We have all the information we need,
and he delivered it straight to our door.

544
00:27:06.100 --> 00:27:11.820
– Prepare for battle!
– Prepare for battle!

545
00:27:12.250 --> 00:27:16.240
Six power masters proceed to land
as soon as the battle begins!

546
00:27:16.320 --> 00:27:19.510
Our mission is to free
the captured Cipher Pol agents!

547
00:27:20.310 --> 00:27:23.250
Artillery fire won't
work on the pacifistas!

548
00:27:23.330 --> 00:27:26.190
Aim all cannons at the sea
beast weapons!

549
00:27:26.190 --> 00:27:27.020
Thunderclap!

550
00:27:36.440 --> 00:27:38.300
The stars will be...

551
00:27:42.660 --> 00:27:43.460
Hahahaha!

552
00:27:43.980 --> 00:27:46.800
I love this place too
but we gotta lock in, bro!

553
00:27:48.720 --> 00:27:50.310
Made it, there's the sunny-

554
00:28:00.650 --> 00:28:02.050
No turning back...

555
00:28:02.880 --> 00:28:05.110
Sacred Yata Mirror.

556
00:28:23.310 --> 00:28:24.390
He's here.

557
00:28:24.780 --> 00:28:25.680
Let's go!

558
00:28:26.380 --> 00:28:27.260
Pacifistas!

559
00:28:43.010 --> 00:28:45.230
I won't go easy on you!

560
00:28:45.610 --> 00:28:51.130
Bring it on, Uncle!

561
00:28:53.060 --> 00:28:55.380
You're facing
the strongest defense...

562
00:28:55.460 --> 00:28:58.730
In the whole world!

563
00:29:06.430 --> 00:29:07.490
What?

564
00:29:10.770 --> 00:29:12.090
What's going on?

565
00:29:12.570 --> 00:29:14.450
Where is this light
coming from?

566
00:29:17.820 --> 00:29:19.090
Someone's here!

567
00:29:20.390 --> 00:29:22.080
Someone strong!
